     1	"""The bound resolver (docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3 and its product-facing
     2	contract; proofs 2b to 2d): one owner for every upper date bound, explicit or omitted.
     3	
     4	On four real store states (`bound_cases.py`) every public function that takes a date is called with an omitted, a past and a future
     5	bound, and each outcome is compared with today's, recorded before the change (`fixtures/bound-baseline-2026-11-16.json`), except where
     6	the contract changes it:
     7	- an explicit bound after the last completed day is refused, naming that day (finished and partial stores);
     8	- a first-day store refuses every call;
     9	- on a store with work after its last completed day, the bundle functions' omitted bound reads as of that day, so the half-processed
    10	  day is no longer returned;
    11	- a range whose start is after its end is refused (council round 124); a start equal to the end reads as before.
    12	Plus the structural check that no module resolves a bound elsewhere, and the API's mapping of the three refusals."""
