   124	    rung = next((g for g in store.rungs_of(ledger, view_id) if g['position'] == state['position']), {})
   125	    result = {'position': state['position'], 'label': rung.get('label', '')}
   245	   - a retry after another day has completed reuses exactly the staged rows whose four key parts match;
   246	   - two stores at the same path with the same first sequence and day but different identities: no staged row of the first is
   247	     reused for the second, and no published vector of the first is used for the second;
   248	   - a store restored from an earlier snapshot, with the same identity but a published day after its last completed day: its
   249	     published vectors are not used until a refresh;
   250	   - a restored store with the same identity and published day but one view's text changed: that view's vector is not used, and
   251	     search runs lexically and says so.
   252	8d. **Orderly stop:** with a service reader holding the store, the writer's stop leaves WAL mode in place, records it and releases the
   253	   lock; preflight then accepts the store. With no reader, the store ends in rollback-journal mode.
   254	8c. **The index:** on a store with an unfinished day, the views sent to the (fake) embedding service are exactly those visible as of
   255	   the last completed day. After the day completes, the index is extended to it, and search names the index's day until then.
